WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.704
One checkout is open. A second cashier is available.

00:00:05.854 --> 00:00:10.688
The line is starting to grow. Do you open another checkout?

00:00:10.838 --> 00:00:14.581
Let's follow one customer and see what makes the wait.

00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:24.125
Here is Ben's visit from the start. He joins the line at nine oh one.

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:28.988
Record his arrival here. His waiting time starts now.

00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:35.553
Cara joins behind Ben.

00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:40.856
The cashier is still helping Ana, so both customers wait in line.

00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:46.645
Ana finishes and leaves. It is Ben's turn.

00:00:46.795 --> 00:00:50.759
When his service begins, which clock should stop?

00:00:55.709 --> 00:00:58.253
His waiting clock stops.

00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:04.527
At nine oh two, the cashier starts serving Ben. Record service start.

00:01:05.977 --> 00:01:08.301
Ben is being served now.

00:01:08.451 --> 00:01:13.965
Only his service clock runs. His waiting time stays at one minute.

00:01:15.477 --> 00:01:20.740
At nine oh four, Ben's service ends. Record that time.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:27.374
He leaves, and Cara moves forward. Ben spent two minutes receiving service.

00:01:30.477 --> 00:01:36.225
Ben spent three minutes here: one minute waiting, then two minutes in service.

00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:41.544
Arrival, service start, and service end explain the difference.

00:01:42.994 --> 00:01:51.822
Lambda describes the arrival rate. Mu describes the service rate of one counter. C counts available counters.

00:01:51.972 --> 00:01:56.985
Queueing theory studies how these parts of the service process relate to waiting.

00:01:59.735 --> 00:02:05.614
If the second checkout is already staffed when Ben arrives, he can start immediately.

00:02:05.764 --> 00:02:09.828
His wait in this example changes from one minute to zero.

00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:17.759
That is the idea behind studying a queue: connect what you observe to the time people spend waiting.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:23.387
Next, we will collect the records behind those numbers in your own workplace.
